WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:07.127
"How to Prevent Wrinkles with Diet"

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:10.760
"Skin Wrinkling:
Can Food Make a Difference?"

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:12.800
Population studies
have found that healthy diets

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:16.200
tend to be associated
with less severe facial aging.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.600
Presumably this is
because unhealthy foods

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:21.280
might increase
the oxidative stress load,

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:21.940
be pro-inflammatory,

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:24.640
and the advanced glycation
end products

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:27.880
I talk about in my video
The Best Diet for Healthy Aging,

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:30.640
whereas healthy foods
might provide protection

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:33.560
by having an inside-out
sunscreen effect,

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:36.560
stimulating collagen production
and DNA repair,

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:37.700
which could help explain why

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:40.200
a meat and junk predominant
eating pattern

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:41.880
was associated
with more wrinkles,

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:43.440
whereas a fruit-dominant pattern

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:44.960
or those eating more fruits,
vegetables,

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:47.480
and nuts
may enjoy less wrinkling.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.000
Vegetables, beans,
and olive oil

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:50.920
appeared protective
versus meat and dairy.

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:53.840
Fish was initially correlated
with less skin wrinkling,

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:55.640
but the association disappeared

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:57.520
upon multiple
regression analyses,

00:00:57.520 --> 00:01:00.520
meaning it was likely
a spurious result

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:03.120
due to fish consumption being
associated with, for example,

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:07.120
other healthy foods such as
salad or cooked vegetables.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:09.200
Higher vitamin C intakes
were associated

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:11.120
with lower odds
of a wrinkled appearance

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:13.960
in a study of 4,000
middle-aged American women.

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:15.600
In terms of specific foods,

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:19.000
yellow and green vegetables
may be particularly protective.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:22.080
The Daniell scale
was used to test the effect

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:24.280
of crow's feet wrinkles
around the eyes

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:26.040
of seven hundred women.

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:28.040
Those eating
less than one daily serving

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:29.280
of green or yellow veggies

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:32.480
averaged about a three
on the Daniell scale,

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:34.360
while women eating
more than two servings a day

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.880
averaged closer to a two.

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:38.400
But maybe people
who go out of their way

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:39.480
to eat more vegetables,

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:43.040
also go out of their way
to wear more sunblock.

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:44.560
Or maybe people
who eat more meat

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:47.080
are out barbequing
in the sun.

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:48.240
Researchers suggest,

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:50.040
"Global disease
prevention strategies

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:52.400
might benefit from emphasizing
that a healthy diet

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:55.120
is also linked
to less facial wrinkling,"

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:59.200
but first we should make sure
to establish cause-and-effect.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:02.440
In my video How to Naturally
Reduce Wrinkles with Food,

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:04.160
I cover interventional studies

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:06.880
showing that two palmfuls
of almonds a day

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:08.920
can both increase
the UV resistance

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:09.760
of people's skin

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:12.760
and decrease wrinkle severity
and width compared to those,

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:16.400
instead,
randomized to nut-free snacks.

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:19.600
What other foods have been shown
to counter skin aging?

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:23.110
The amount of flaxseed oil found
in a daily 3/4 of a tablespoon

00:02:23.110 --> 00:02:24.560
(11.25 g) of ground flaxseeds

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:26.640
significantly increased
skin smoothness

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:29.360
compared to placebo
within six weeks.

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:31.200
In vitro, sulforaphane,

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:33.560
the cruciferous compound
in broccoli,

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:36.320
is able to mitigate
the premature skin aging

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:40.240
induced by air pollution
particulate matter in vitro,

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:42.160
but it has not been
put to the test.

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:45.960
But a component of soy foods
has been tested.

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:49.000
Postmenopausal women
were given four servings a day

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:52.800
of soy foods worth
of isoflavones for six months.

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:55.000
Unfortunately,
there was no control group,

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:56.720
but they did take skin biopsies

00:02:56.720 --> 00:02:58.840
from their butts
before and after

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:00.360
and found
a significant improvement

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:01.520
in skin thickness,

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:03.320
along with increased
collagen content

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:06.040
and elastic fibers.

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:07.920
How about
a randomized controlled trial

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:10.160
with a more modest soy intake?

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:14.080
About a serving and a half a day
of soy's worth of isoflavones

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:17.760
was pitted against placebo
in middle-aged women.

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:20.780
Facial skin elasticity
improved by week 8,

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:22.680
and an improvement
in fine wrinkles

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:24.720
was noted by week 12.

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:27.560
Another 12-week study
using equol directly,

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:29.440
which is a compound
that good gut bacteria

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:32.000
can turn soy isoflavones into,

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:35.200
found a significant reduction
in wrinkle depth,

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:38.320
though you have to have
the right gut bugs.

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:43.280
See my video How to Convert
Into an Equol Producer.

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:46.080
The only other interventional
food study on wrinkles

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:50.800
I could find tested one
of my favorite fruits: mangoes.

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:54.600
Feeding mango to mice reduced
UV-induced wrinkle formation,

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:58.760
but it wasn't put to the test
in people until 2020.

00:03:58.760 --> 00:04:00.600
Light-skinned
postmenopausal women

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:02.680
were randomized to eat
about a half cup (120 ml)

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:05.400
of champagne mango or around
a cup and a half (360 ml)

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:07.120
every day for 16 weeks.

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:08.760
Lucky ducks!

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:11.120
Unfortunately,
as an exploratory study,

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:13.960
there was no usual
diet control group,

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:16.920
but compared to baseline,
the deep-wrinkle severity

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:19.960
in the half-cup group
significantly decreased

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:23.120
by week eight and remained so
for the duration of the study.

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:27.680
In contrast, to the funding
National Mango Board's chagrin,

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:29.840
average wrinkle severity
got worse

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:32.960
by the end of the 16 weeks
in the cup and a half group.

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:34.160
The researchers suggested

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:36.440
it might have been due
to the extra sugar intake,

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:38.160
but there wasn't
actually any changes

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:42.080
in blood sugar levels,
so it remains a mystery.

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:44.280
The paucity
of interventional trials

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:47.320
limits the confidence one
can put into recommendations,

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:51.600
but the best approximation
for an anti-wrinkle diet

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:54.440
would be one naturally rich
in antioxidants,

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:55.960
anti-inflammatory,

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:58.040
and would limit sugar spikes
and glycation

00:04:58.040 --> 00:05:01.360
both by limiting added sugars
and refined carbs,

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:04.080
and avoiding preformed
advanced glycation end products

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:06.480
found in fried,
grilled, and broiled meats.

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:09.280
In other words, when patients
inquire about a diet

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:12.000
that might contribute
to younger-looking skin,

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:13.520
evidence supports
the recommendation

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:29.480
to follow a whole foods,
plant-based diet.

